{
  _comment: "Canonical Taiwu terms (EN->RU) handed to the engine to enforce, grouped by meaning. Matched case-insensitively as whole words; only terms in a unit are sent. Yandex applies them via its native glossary with exact:false (it DECLINES each term to fit Russian grammar); LM Studio gets them in the prompt with the same instruction. Give the dictionary (nominative) RU form (e.g. Sect->секта); the engine inflects it. CASE MATTERS: the engine copies the value's leading letter into mid-sentence output, so use mid-sentence case — lowercase for common nouns, capital only for proper names (Инь, Дао, sect/city names). Editing a value re-translates exactly the texts containing the term (per-text srcHash/cache signature); bump GLOSSARY_VERSION in src/config/glossary.ts only to force a FULL re-translation. Keys starting with '_' are ignored; '_section_*' keys are human-readable group headers (surfaced as divider rows in the CSV export). A value may be a bare RU string, or an object {ru, feed}: 'feed' is an engine-facing surrogate used when the raw term breaks the MT engine (e.g. the period in 'Phy.' is read by Yandex as a sentence boundary, splitting the term); the dot-free surrogate ('Physical Penetration') is fed to Yandex in both the text and the glossary pair so matching and declension work, then the RU value comes back declined. (Chinese source terms were dropped from this file; see git history for the {ru,cn} form.)",

